{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: Worker pin can't detect a regression to *silent* swallow**

The new worker test pins the "swallow does not mask the envelope" half — if the worker ever reverted to *propagating*, `.wait()` would throw and this test would go red. Good.

But the other direction is unpinned: if the swallow ever lost its log line (reverted to `catch (_) {}`), this test still passes — the stderr log is the only observable for the swallow half, and nothing asserts it. Cross-checking: a total "drain no-ops" regression *is* caught by the main-engine test (the run would stop failing), so the residual gap is only silent-swallow.

If you want the pin airtight, give the timer an out-of-band observable before it throws, e.g.:

```javascript
function () {
  setTimeout(function () {
    console.warn('late-timer-fired');   // visible on stderr during the test
    throw new Error('late-boom');
  }, 0);
  return 42;
}
```

and (if practical) assert the log via a captured stderr stream. Even a source-level comment acknowledging the limitation would help future readers of this pin.
